I don't think holding a lizard corpse will protect you from touching
a cockatrice corpse.  Eating a lizard corpse may revive you when you're
turning to stone.

You can pick it up if you are wearing gloves.  I think what you are 
talking about is only a problem if you are blind.  Then you have to 
to feel what is on the ground before trying to pick it up.  If
you can see, you can just look and see the corpse there.

I thought that you could pick up the rest of the stuff in the pile 
without touching the corpse -- just say no when it asks you if you want
to pick it up.  (warning: I haven't tried this).

Also, the corpse wouldn't sit there forever -- it would rot eventually.
